      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 1–2 at% Mo will produce fine Mo-rich precipitates in the lamellar matrix.",
      "field": "hypothesis; structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-rich precipitates will be uniformly distributed.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-rich precipitates will obstruct dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-rich precipitates will stabilize the microstructure against coarsening during thermal and mechanical exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-rich precipitates will stabilize the microstructure against phase separation during thermal and mechanical exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitate-mediated obstruction and stabilization will enhance alloy strength.",
      "field": "mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitate-mediated obstruction and stabilization will reduce creep strain and improve creep resistance under sustained loading.",
      "field": "mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo addition will promote formation of a more protective surface passive layer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Improved passivation will lower the corrosion rate of the alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-modified alloy will have a better strength–ductility balance than unmodified AlCoCrFeNi2.1.",
      "field": "hypothesis; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted improvements will occur without sacrificing ductility.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The improvements require controlled Mo content near 1–2 at% and processing that preserves the uniform lamellar structure.",
